### 2.8 `app/api/` — HTTP Endpoints

#### `records.py`

Three endpoints, all read-only, all using FastAPI dependency injection for session management:

| Endpoint | SQL | Schema |
|----------|-----|--------|
| `GET /records/` | `SELECT ... ORDER BY last_seen DESC LIMIT/OFFSET` with optional `WHERE source=? AND status=?` | `RegulatoryRecordBrief` (no raw_content) |
| `GET /records/{id}` | `SELECT ... WHERE id=?` | `RegulatoryRecordOut` (full raw_content) |
| `GET /records/{id}/history` | `SELECT ... WHERE record_id=? ORDER BY detected_at DESC` | `ChangeEventOut` (includes diff_summary) |

**Design note**: The list endpoint supports pagination (`limit`/`offset`) and filtering (`source`, `status`) via query parameters. No full-text search — that would require a separate search index (Postgres `tsvector` or Elasticsearch).

#### `scrape.py`

A single `POST /scrape` endpoint. Delegates to `run_scrape_pipeline()`, commits on success, rolls back on failure. The endpoint is thin — all business logic lives in `scrape_pipeline.py`.

#### `webhooks.py`

Five endpoints, all thin wrappers around `_register()` and `_list_subs()` helpers:

| Method | Path | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| `POST` | `/webhooks` | Register |
| `GET` | `/webhooks` | List (with `?active_only=true`) |
| `POST` | `/webhooks/subscribe` | Register (alias) |
| `GET` | `/webhooks/subscriptions` | List (alias) |
| `DELETE` | `/webhooks/subscriptions/{id}` | Hard-delete |

**Design note**: The alias paths exist for backward compatibility. The original API had `/webhooks/subscribe` and `/webhooks/subscriptions`. The new shorter paths are the canonical ones.

